SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: AI Powered Women
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEve
 nt URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/182250\n\n5:30PM Reception
 \, 6:00PM Discussion\nAI is reshaping the world - but who is shaping AI?\n
 \nThis discussion brings together leading women at the forefront of artifi
 cial intelligence to explore the human decisions\, ethical frameworks\, an
 d leadership required to guide this moment of rapid transformation.\n\nDr.
  Felicia Newhouse\, founder of AI-Powered Women—a global learning platfo
 rm and 1\,200-person MIT summit focused on building the workforce infrastr
 ucture behind responsible AI adoption—will share insights on how organiz
 ations translate AI investment into real-world implementation\, where lead
 ership\, culture\, and human capability determine success. She is joined b
 y Dr. Karrie Karahalios of the MIT Media Lab\, a pioneer in algorithmic ac
 countability\, and Dr. Cansu Canca\, Director of Responsible AI Practice a
 t Northeastern University and founder of AI Ethics Lab and creator of Puz
 zle-solving in Ethics (PiE) Model.\n\nTogether\, they will examine how AI 
 systems reflect the values and assumptions of those who build and deploy t
 hem and why diverse leadership is not just important\, but essential. From
  bias and governance to trust\, identity\, and decision-making\, the conve
 rsation moves beyond technology to the deeper question of responsibility.\
 n\nAn intimate\, interdisciplinary conversation on women shaping the futur
 e of AI and the systems that will shape us all.\n\n*This event is complime
 ntary and reserved for members only. Light bites and refreshments will be 
 served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/182250
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
