LOCATION:Offsite: New York City
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: $420.56 per person\nAvailability: 4 
 spots left\nStatus: Available\nTime: 9 AM – 5 PM\nEvent URL: https://mem
 bers.thequinhouse.com/events/184226\n\nWe are excited to offer a curated\,
  behind-the-scenes look at the contemporary art world lead by The ’Quin 
 House art curator\, Kate Chertavian.\n\nSpend a private morning at Christi
 e’s\, featuring expert insights from leading specialists in Impressionis
 t\, Modern\, and 20th Century art. Through guided discussion and close loo
 king\, members will gain a deeper understanding of the auction process and
  highlights of the May sales.\n\nFrom there\, members will travel to Chels
 ea for a series of guided gallery visits at David Zwirner\, Hales\, and Ha
 user & Wirth\, where you will experience current exhibitions at some of th
 e most influential galleries in the world.\n\nMidday\, members will gather
  for a lunch discussion with Kate\, focused on strategies for navigating a
 n art fair and building a thoughtful approach to collecting.\n\nThe aftern
 oon will conclude at Frieze New York at The Shed\, where members will have
  the opportunity to explore the fair independently\, applying insights fro
 m the day in real time. Throughout the experience\, members will gain behi
 nd-the-scenes perspective on the art market\, along with Kate’s “5 Thi
 ngs to Know about Collecting.”\n\n9:00AM - 9:15AM | Arrival & Welcome at
  Christie’s\n9:15AM - 11:00AM | Private Viewing at Christie’s\n11:00AM
  - 11:30AM | Transit to Chelsea\n11:30AM - 1:20PM | Gallery Visits: David 
 Zwirner\, Hales\, Hauser & Wirth\n1:30PM - 2:30PM | Lunch & Discussion wit
 h Kate Chertavian\n3:00PM - 5:00PM | Independent Browsing at Frieze New Yo
 rk\n\nThis intimate\, thoughtfully designed program offers a unique opport
 unity to engage directly with experts\, deepen your understanding of the a
 rt market\, and experience New York’s art scene alongside fellow members
 .\n\n*This excursion is offered to members-only at $450 per person\, inclu
 ding the cost of lunch\, group transportation between Christie's and the g
 alleries\, as well as your ticket to the Frieze Art Fair. A limited number
  of spaces are available on a first come\, first to reserve basis. Members
  are responsible for their own transportation to and from New York. Ticke
 ts are non-refundable and non-transferable.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/184226
CATEGORIES:The Arts
