BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-184208@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260518T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260518T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260518T190000
SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "Love & Other Monsters" with Emily Frank
 lin
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 49 spots left\nS
 tatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/1842
 08\n\nBookmark the date for a captivating conversation exploring Love & O
 ther Monsters by Emily Franklin—a richly imagined novel set against the 
 haunting backdrop of the “Year Without Summer.”\n\nIn 1816\, amid unre
 lenting storms on the shores of Lake Geneva\, a group of young literary ic
 ons—including Mary and Percy Shelley and the infamous Lord Byron—gathe
 r to create\, provoke\, and unravel. At the center of it all is Claire Cla
 irmont: clever\, passionate\, and often overshadowed\, yet determined to c
 arve out her own identity in a world dominated by brilliance and ego. As r
 omance\, rivalry\, and ambition collide\, Claire must navigate loyalty\, l
 onging\, and the cost of living—and loving—on the edge of history.\n\n
 Blending historical intrigue with emotional depth\, Love & Other Monsters
  explores the origins of legendary works like Frankenstein while giving vo
 ice to the woman too often left out of the story.\n\nJoin us for an engagi
 ng discussion moderated by Wendy Dodson\, owner of Hummingbird Books\, as 
 we delve into this atmospheric novel and its themes of creativity\, fame\,
  and the monsters we make—both real and imagined.\n\n*This event is comp
 limentary and reserved for members only. Light refreshments will be served
 .
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/184208
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
