UID:quin-event-183090@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260704T150000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260704
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260707
SUMMARY:'Venture: Wimbledon
LOCATION:Offsite
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Venture - Travel\nPrice: $12850.47 per person\nSta
 tus: Available\nTime: 3 PM – 12 PM\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinho
 use.com/events/183090\n\nAn Exclusive Seat at Tennis' Most Iconic Stage. E
 xperience the Prestige of Wimbledon.\nMore than a visit to London\, this i
 s an invitation to one of sport’s most rarefied worlds - Wimbledon... wh
 ere tradition\, precision\, and quiet luxury converge on perfectly kept gr
 ass courts.\n\nYour weekend centers on Sunday at the All England Lawn Tenn
 is Club\, where members will take their place on Centre Court with coveted
  Debenture tickets\, among the most exclusive seats in global sport. As th
 e Championships enter the fourth round\, the atmosphere sharpens: the fiel
 d narrows\, the stakes heighten\, and the game reveals its most compelling
  drama. From this vantage point\, members will witness the world’s fines
 t players in matches that will define the trajectory to the finals.\n\nBet
 ween play\, move at your own pace through the grounds - where champagne is
  poured with ease\, strawberries and cream remain a ritual\, and every det
 ail reflects Wimbledon’s singular blend of heritage and refinement. This
  is not simply spectating\; it is participation in a cultural institution\
 , experienced as it was intended.\n\nCurated with intention\, this is an i
 nsider experience of Wimbledon at its most electric\, shared in the compan
 y of those who appreciate it most.\n\nDay One | Saturday\, July 4th\n\nYou
 r journey begins with your arrival in London\, where you will be welcomed 
 to The Kensington Hotel\, a refined townhouse known for its polished discr
 etion and residential charm.\n\nOnce checked in\, take a moment to unwind 
 from your travels - whether relaxing in the hotel’s inviting drawing roo
 ms or stepping out to explore the surrounding neighborhood at your leisure
 . The afternoon is yours to ease into the rhythm of the city or connect wi
 th fellow ‘Quin members as the experience unofficially begins.\n\nIn the
  evening\, gather for a 'Quin Member welcome dinner hosted by former-Londo
 ner - our very own Managing Director\, Matthias Kiehm at The Audley Public
  House. The Audley is a proper neighborhood Pub where history and contempo
 rary art collide. Here\, amid thoughtfully restored interiors and a conviv
 ial atmosphere\, members will be reintroduced to fellow fans of the sport 
 over a beautifully prepared dinner while anticipating the next days matche
 s.\n\nDay Two | Sunday\, July 5th\n\nYour second day begins with a seamles
 s departure from The Kensington Hotel as you make your way to Wimbledon\, 
 with travel arrangements thoughtfully coordinated for ease and comfort.\n\
 nUpon arrival at the All England Lawn Tennis Club on "Middle Sunday\," you
  will have the full day to experience the Gentlemen's and Ladies' Singles 
 Fourth Round at your own pace. With Debenture ticket(s) in hand\, enjoy pr
 ime seating on Centre Court - where the field narrows and the tournament�
 �s momentum becomes palpable. Your tickets also provide access to No. 1 Co
 urt and the outer courts\, allowing you to move fluidly between matches an
 d take in the breadth of play across the grounds.\n\nThroughout the day\, 
 you will have access to the Debenture Holders’ Lounge and its collection
  of private bars and dining venues. Whether pausing for a leisurely lunch\
 , a glass of champagne\, or a moment of respite overlooking the courts\, t
 he experience is yours to shape as you wish.\n\nFollowing the conclusion o
 f play\, return to London in the early evening. Keeping dynamic match time
 s in mind\, the day concludes with a relaxed late-evening group dinner\, i
 n a stylish yet comfortable setting to unwind and reflect before returning
  to The Kensington Hotel for a well-deserved nights rest.\n\nDay Three | M
 onday\, July 6th\n\nYour final morning begins at a relaxed pace with break
 fast at The Kensington Hotel. Enjoy a quiet start to the day - whether ove
 r a leisurely meal or a final moment of calm in the hotel’s inviting sur
 roundings.\n\nFollowing breakfast\, departures will take place on your own
  schedule - whether returning home\, or staying on for an independent exte
 nsion to the trip. As you make your way home\, carry with you the memories
  of a weekend defined by exceptional access\, thoughtful curation\, and th
 e shared experience of Wimbledon at its most compelling.\n\nClassic Room |
  Single Occupancy\n\nClassic Room at The Kensington Hotel | Two Twin Beds
  with Breakfast Included\n\nOne Wimbledon Debenture Ticket to the Gentlem
 en's and Ladies' Singles Fourth Round\, including Centre Court seating and
  the Debenture's Holders' Lounge with its collection of private bars and d
 ining venues.\n\nTwo curated group dinners\, including a welcome dinner at
  The Audley Public House.\n\n$7\,950\n\nClassic Room | Double Occupancy\n\
 nClassic Room at The Kensington Hotel | Queen Bed with Breakfast Included\
 n\nTwo Wimbledon Debenture Tickets to the Gentlemen's and Ladies' Singles 
 Fourth Round\, including Centre Court seating and the Debenture's Holders'
  Lounge with its collection of private bars and dining venues.\n\nTwo cura
 ted group dinners\, including a welcome dinner at The Audley Public House.
 \n\n$13\,750\n\nPlease note the price of airfare is not included in the ti
 cket price. Members and their guests are responsible for booking their own
  flights. For the smoothest arrival experience\, we recommend flying into 
 London Heathrow Airport (LHR) located less than an hour by car from The Ke
 nsington Hotel.\n\n* Reservations are non-refundable and non-transferable.
  Please note that all bookings are subject to the terms and conditions out
 lined in the final confirmation materials including your sign-off on a sta
 ndard liability waiver.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/183090
CATEGORIES:‘Venture - Travel
END:VEVENT
